  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When using the color mask, each channel does not mix within the color mask. Each channel is applied in RGBA order. For example, If the green channel overlaps with the red channel, even if the green channel's color is set to black in additive mode (or white in multiply mode), the green areas will still be masked out of the red channel.\n\nExpected behavior is that the channels will blend with themselves using the mode set for the color mask, rather than layer on top of each other.\n\nAn alternative solution would be to have sliders controlling the mask linear blending for each channel, which would still have them stack, but would allow layers to be disabled or smoothly blended between.\n\nFor",
